+    feat(storage): DB-GAP-051 segment consolidation + oversize split (JSONL repair path)
+    
+    Adds the missing segment-level repair path. Before this, the only compaction
+    (squashPartition/compactHistory) converted a WHOLE partition to Parquet and
+    skipped young partitions, so neither defect had a JSONL-preserving fix:
+    
+      - 16,240 near-empty numeric segments in scheduler/event/2026-09 (a 150-file
+        sample was 1 line each);
+      - segments far past the 1000-line / 1MB rotation bound left by the
+        DB-GAP-049 9999 freeze (the same partition's 10000.jsonl at 88,206 lines /
+        84,677,070 bytes).
+    
+    src/storage/segment-consolidation.ts plans and applies merges and splits while
+    keeping the partition JSONL. Records are never re-serialized and never
+    re-ordered (compareChunkNames order, imported from ./jsonl so the comparator
+    cannot drift), the total record count is asserted BEFORE any deletion,
+    replacement content is written before any input is removed, an existing
+    segment name is never overwritten, and the operation is idempotent.
+    
+    CLI: `duckbrain squash --segments --partition=<domain/YYYY-MM> [--dry-run]`.
+    --partition is required and never inferred (there is no "all partitions" mode
+    for a pass that rewrites and deletes files).
+    
+    Verification (foreman, independent of the worker):
+      - merge on copies of 300 real 1-line segments: 300 files -> 1, records
+        300 -> 300, record sequence byte-identical;
+      - split of a copy of the real 84MB segment: 1 file -> 130 files, records
+        88,206 -> 88,206, record sequence byte-identical, 0 segments over bound;
+      - dry run wrote nothing; a second execute reported nothing to do
+        (dir listing + mtimes unchanged);
+      - prod namespaces/ fingerprint unchanged (file count + dirlist sha + big
+        file sha) and git status shows no namespaces/ entry;
+      - new suite src/storage/segment-consolidation.test.ts 15/15 solo;
+      - tsc --noEmit exit 0; prettier --check src/ clean.
+    
+    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
